# Patch:        030-field-cfg-rpitit-packed-methods
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       field/src/packed/packed_traits.rs, matrix/src/lib.rs, baby-bear/tests/pre_patch_030.rs
# Hunks:        6
# Class:        cfg-hide
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 10 (charon#1266, as for 020), and 9 for
#               `unpack_iter`'s mixed type/function recursion group. Without
#               the `unpack_iter` hunk aeneas stops on p3-baby-bear ("Mixed-
#               recursive declaration groups are not supported", "Can not
#               extract trait associated types with parameters"). Without the
#               three `PackedFieldExtension` hunks the generated Lean is the
#               same, but charon prints 12 "GATs cannot work with
#               `--lift-associated-types`" warnings.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: every change is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant, four default
#               methods are absent and `to_ext_iter` sits on an extension trait.
# Upstreamable: yes: inert in a normal build, but it adds an extractor-only
#               trait to p3-field and an import to p3-matrix; charon#1266 is the
#               better fix.
# Drop when:    as for 020.
# Test:         test p3-baby-bear --test pre_patch_030
# Mutation:     `unpack_ext_iter` is gated on the wrong cfg, so a normal build
#               lacks it.
#
# Same root cause as 020, but these traits cannot be cut loose, because
# `Field::Packing: PackedField` is load-bearing. Four default methods return
# `impl Iterator`, so each one adds a hidden GAT to `PackedValue` or
# `PackedFieldExtension`. `unpack_iter`'s closure also forms a mixed
# type/function recursion group with `PackedValue`, which aeneas rejects on
# its own terms.
#
# Under cfg(hax_backend_lean) only:
#   PackedValue::unpack_iter                        absent
#   PackedFieldExtension::unpack_ext_iter           absent
#   PackedFieldExtension::packed_ext_powers_capped  absent
#   PackedFieldExtension::to_ext_iter               moved, same body, to a
#                                                   blanket extension trait
#                                                   `PackedFieldExtensionIter`
# `to_ext_iter` is called by p3-matrix, which is in p3-baby-bear's graph (via
# p3-mds), so under the cfg it moves rather than disappears, and p3-matrix
# imports the trait under the same cfg. Charon only translates dependency
# items that are reachable, and nothing reachable from p3-baby-bear uses the
# new trait, so it never reaches aeneas.
#
# In a normal build none of this exists: the methods are where they were,
# unchanged, and upstream's callers and tests (field-testing, fri, stir,
# sumcheck, multilinear-util, …) compile and run against them as shipped.
# Under the cfg, rustc checks that nothing reachable still uses an absent
# method (see 020).
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
